A||||5||88formula||Straightforward questions on the 3.4 60 v6???||||3||
Z||000000||88formula||01-29-2000||06:23 PM||||This is for the fieroholics here that have the 3.4 pushrod engine ALREADY in their fieros. I did a search on this subject and found most of the threads to be ambiguous. I want to know things like real dyno results, performance numbers like 0-60 times and 1/4 mile times, how drivable it is, cost of the swap, modifications you did, and any other pertinent information that will help me make a decision on the 3.4 engine swap. I already know about the starter relocation and the modifications that need to be done that I learned from Ed Parks Fiero Factory <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/Page1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/Page1.html</A>  and the threads that were posted on this forum <BR>Please, NO comments or comparisons about how the 3.2 engine is cheaper or better than the 3.4. If any of you guys with the 3.4 engine could answer any one of these questions that would be great. <P>Cliff, I read in a thread that you were doing a 3.4 engine swap.  ||||reg||3
Z||000001||fierosound||01-29-2000||07:36 PM||||I hear ya...   I've also been considering a 3.4 swap in the near future as well and have been doing research.  However, I didn't want to wind up with only 20 more horses (as with the GM 3.4L crate engine's 160hp) for all that hard work and money.<P>The BEST information I've come up for a performance  combination is at the site below.  It is a 3.4L , using pistons for the 3.4 TDC (DOHC) engine (to get the compression ratio up) and cast iron heads.   I think I'll be following this lead, perhaps with a more agressive cam.<P> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/NewProject.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/NewProject.html</A> ||||reg||10
